message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "LAT-S2 pilot: Jacobian-lens monitor and text-stated norms in Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikabri88-cmd/lat-s2-pilot"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ryzhkova
    given-names: Julia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4194-6059"
    affiliation: Siriona
    email: research@siriona.one
abstract: >-
  Exploratory pilot that carried the LAT-S1b measures of monitor visibility over to Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct with a
  Jacobian-lens (J-lens) monitor. Twelve norms that flip a reported device state were tested on two devices with 96
  items each. The model followed 21 of 24 norm-device pairs; among them the lens showed 8-9 sighted norms and no blind
  norm at any monitored layer, and an independently fitted community lens agreed wherever both read the fact. The
  decision rule fixed before the run required at least three blind norms, so LAT-S2 stops in its current form. An
  audit of the probe-lens gap at layer 13 traced it to input information present before the answer forms. The
  release holds the pilot note, code, the Colab notebook, the main-run summary and log, and the audit scripts,
  outputs and arrays.
